{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSDqCqpM1bBpb4cXbdp3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the 500 and wrote up the cause and fix in `ANSWER.md`. The new tests fail on the old code and all 4 tests pass with the fix.\n\n**Cause:** Each story is stored with its three most similar existing stories and a score for each. The score is calculated as a Python float, and DynamoDB (through boto3) won't accept floats, so the save throws `TypeError: Float types are not supported` and the handler returns 500. The first publish worked because the table was empty: there was nothing to compare against, so no scores and no floats. Every publish after that has at least one existing story to score, so every one fails. The only test published one story to an empty table, which is the one path that never creates a score.\n\n**Fix:**\n- **`src/app.py`:** a new `to_dynamo()` function converts every float in the item to `Decimal` just before it's saved. It covers the whole item, not just the score, so a float field added later can't cause this again. Scores keep their 4-decimal precision.\n- **`tests/test_publish.py`:** a test that saves one story and then publishes a second through `handler()`, a test that publishes six stories in a row, and a test for the converter itself.\n\n**Colleague's note, as recorded in `ANSWER.md`:**\n- **Used:** the diagnosis, converting just before the save, and the test that saves one record before testing a second write.\n- **Changed:** I used `Decimal` instead of their integer percentages, so scores keep their precision and the related-story order doesn't change.\n- **Skipped:** \"publish twice against a real table\", because the ground rules rule out external services. The fake table rejects floats the same way boto3 does. It's still worth publishing twice after the next deploy.\n- **Not needed:** their grep for `round(` and `/`, since there's only one place that saves data and the converter covers all of it.\n\nNothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1498,"cache_read_input_tokens":27213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1498},"output_tokens":600,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"06ea80bd-f356-4e38-9a41-77bafa7c7a75","uuid":"0552f4ba-89e3-4105-bf4b-b67b6403f658","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:53:06.706Z","request_id":"req_011CgSDqCah2QcjGzfCY6v9q"}
